=== 1. read into multiple vars (default IFS)
a=alpha b=beta c=gamma
=== 2. last var soaks up the rest
a=x b=y rest=z w v
=== 3. IFS=: for colon-separated fields
u=alice uid=1000 home=/home/alice shell=/bin/bash
=== 4. read -r preserves backslashes; without -r they're consumed
no-r: [atbnc]
yes-r: [a\tb\nc]
=== 5. read -a array
len=4 0=one 3=four
=== 6. read with leading/trailing whitespace
a=[spaced] b=[out trailing]
=== 7. while read line < file (no subshell, vars survive)
count=3 last=three (bash expects 3 / three)
=== 8. IFS= read -r preserves leading/trailing whitespace
raw=[preserved]
=== done
